IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il44-nouns`
IMPORT `il44-references`
IMPORT `il44-stale-citations`

-- Row il-44. The sound citation by address (C8), where each side was read, the waiting periods that agree, and the days, as assertions that hold.
-- The citations and the period that do not hold are in `il44-tests-expected-red-stale-citations.l4`.

§ `The control points at what it says`

#ASSERT `the citation by address points at what it says` `citation C8: section 12A1(a) to section 12(a)(1)`

§ `Where the matter now stands is where a sound citation points`

-- S3 means paragraph (1) of section 12, which stands at the address C8 cites.
#ASSERT `citation S3: First Schedule item 4(c) to section 12(1)`'s `the matter the citing words mean now stands at` EQUALS `citation C8: section 12A1(a) to section 12(a)(1)`'s `the citing words give the address`
-- The two defective citations give an address other than the one where the matter now stands.
#ASSERT NOT (`citation S2: regulation 21 to section 13(a)`'s `the citing words give the address` EQUALS `citation S2: regulation 21 to section 13(a)`'s `the matter the citing words mean now stands at`)
#ASSERT NOT (`citation S3: First Schedule item 4(c) to section 12(1)`'s `the citing words give the address` EQUALS `citation S3: First Schedule item 4(c) to section 12(1)`'s `the matter the citing words mean now stands at`)

§ `Where each side of a citation was read`

-- CONSOLIDATION-ONLY: the words of regulation 21.
#ASSERT `citation S2: regulation 21 to section 13(a)`'s `the citing words were read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`
#ASSERT `citation S2: regulation 21 to section 13(a)`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read from the page image of the official instrument`
#ASSERT `citation S3: First Schedule item 4(c) to section 12(1)`'s `the citing words were read` EQUALS `read from the page image of the official instrument`
-- CONSOLIDATION-ONLY: the content of section 12(a) as it stands.
#ASSERT `citation S3: First Schedule item 4(c) to section 12(1)`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`
-- CONSOLIDATION-ONLY: the three days of regulation 21.
#ASSERT `period P1: regulation 21`'s `the period was read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`
#ASSERT `period P2: section 13(d)`'s `the period was read` EQUALS `read from the page image of the official instrument`
#ASSERT `period P3: section 13(d) as read by the 2026 temporary provision for the class of persons in section 13(e)`'s `the period was read` EQUALS `read from the page image of the official instrument`

§ `The regulation and the section give the same period before the temporary variation`

#ASSERT `the two texts give the same period` `period P1: regulation 21` `period P2: section 13(d)`

§ `The days`

-- Amendment 9 was published before it took effect, and the two bounds of that day are in order.
#ASSERT `the day Sefer HaChukim 1804 was published` LESS THAN `the earliest first day of force of Amendment 9`
#ASSERT `the earliest first day of force of Amendment 9` AT MOST `the latest first day of force of Amendment 9`
-- The order of schedule item 4(c) (2014) was published after Amendment 9 and before Amendment 42 (SH 3441, 13.7.2025).
#ASSERT `the latest first day of force of Amendment 9` LESS THAN `the day Kovetz HaTakanot 7386 was published`
#ASSERT `the day Kovetz HaTakanot 7386 was published` LESS THAN `the day Sefer HaChukim 3441 was published`
-- The temporary provision was published in 2026 and, on the bounds read, had not run out on the day this row was written.
#ASSERT `the day Sefer HaChukim 3441 was published` LESS THAN `the day Sefer HaChukim 3506 was published`
#ASSERT `the day Sefer HaChukim 3506 was published` LESS THAN `the day this row was written`
#ASSERT `the day this row was written` LESS THAN `the earliest last day of the period of section 13(e)`
#ASSERT `the earliest last day of the period of section 13(e)` AT MOST `the latest last day of the period of section 13(e)`
